4.1 Applications for Port Access Badges shall be made by the employing company or organisation, not by the individual applicant. Individual applications will not be accepted.

4.2 Applications shall be submitted to the Port Security Unit on Form PSU-01 (Application for Port Access Badge), which may be obtained from the Port Security Unit office at the Apapa Gate Complex or downloaded from the Lagos Port Authority website.

4.3 Each application shall be accompanied by the following documentation:

a) A completed Form PSU-01, signed by the applicant and by an authorised officer of the employing company;

b) Two (2) recent passport photographs of the applicant, with the applicant's name and date of birth written on the reverse of each photograph;

c) A clear photocopy of the applicant's valid means of identification (National Identity Card, International Passport, or Valid Driver's Licence);

d) A letter of introduction from the employing company, on the company's letterhead, stating the applicant's full name, date of birth, designated role, and the specific terminals or areas to which access is required;

e) Evidence of the applicant's employment, such as a letter of appointment or a staff identity card;

f) A completed security questionnaire, as set out in Form PSU-02.

4.4 Applications for vehicle passes shall be submitted on Form PSU-03 (Application for Vehicle Access Pass) and shall be accompanied by:

a) A valid Certificate of Roadworthiness for the vehicle;

b) Evidence of valid motor vehicle insurance;

c) A copy of the vehicle's registration documents;

"Harbor Master" means the officer appointed by the Lagos Port Authority to exercise the powers and duties of the Harbor Master under the Port Act and subsidiary legislation, currently Captain Chidi Okafor.

"Port" means the Lagos Port Complex, including the Tin Can Island Port and the Lekki Deep Sea Port, and all waters, approaches, and anchorages under the jurisdiction of the Lagos Port Authority.

"Vessel Arrival Notification" means the notice required to be submitted under Section 3 of this Directive, comprising the Notice of Readiness and the Pre-Arrival Security Information.

3. VESSEL ARRIVAL NOTIFICATION

3.1 Not later than seventy-two (72) hours before the ETA of a vessel, the Agent shall submit to the Harbor Master's Office:

a) A completed Vessel Arrival Notification form, as set out in Appendix A to this Directive;

b) A copy of the vessel's International Ship Security Certificate (ISSC) or, where the vessel is not required to hold an ISSC, a statement of security arrangements signed by the Master;

c) A copy of the vessel's last port clearance and, if applicable, the Suez Canal or Panama Canal transit certificate;

d) The crew list, passenger list (if any), and the last ten (10) ports of call;

e) A copy of the vessel's Certificate of Registry, Classification Certificate, and International Tonnage Certificate; and

f) Such other information as the Harbor Master may reasonably require to assess the safety and security of the proposed berthing.

3.2 The Pre-Arrival Security Information shall be submitted not later than twenty-four (24) hours before the ETA and shall include:

a) The vessel's International Ship and Port Facility Security (ISPS) Code compliance level;

